2026-09-27T07:58:23.1670710Z Description:
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1671209Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1671658Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1672820Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1674179Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1674302Z Update Note
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1674581Z ===========
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1674995Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1675404Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1675559Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1675877Z ================
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1676055Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1676283Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1676819Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1677152Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1677326Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1677755Z ====================================
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1678031Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1678416Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1678988Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1679522Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1680512Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1681352Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1681509Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1682228Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1683135Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1683651Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1684149Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1684863Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1684997Z Packages
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1685287Z ========
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1685472Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1687629Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1690972Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1691362Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1692173Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1693449Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1694466Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1780396Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1781466Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1782425Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1782597Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1783046Z ==========================
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1783316Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1784950Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1786747Z 
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1787710Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1789261Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T07:58:23.1789581Z 
